  "question": {
    "text": "Let the equations of the sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;of a quadrilateral&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> respectively. If <math><mi>θ</mi></math> is the angle between the diagonals <math><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
